## 11. Troubleshooting

| Problem | What to do |
|---|---|
| `404` on `/api/dashboard/summary` | Verify `NRDADashboardController.java` is under the correct package; restart Monitoring Service |
| `500` on dashboard API | Check MySQL connectivity, `self_healing_db`, `experiment_results` schema, and server logs |
| `JdbcTemplate` bean missing | Ensure `spring-boot-starter-jdbc` is in Monitoring Service `pom.xml`; reload Maven |
| `npm install` gives `EJSONPARSE` | Ensure `package.json` contains one valid JSON object, not two concatenated objects |
| Port `5173` / `5174` already in use | Open the existing Vite URL or stop the old Vite process; use a different port if needed |
| Dashboard opens but has no data | Confirm Monitoring Service `:8083`, API `/summary`, and Vite `/api` proxy |
| Fault Lab returns `403` | Enable `dashboard.fault-controls-enabled=true` locally and restart Monitoring Service |
| Product Service shows `TIMEOUT` during fault | Expected possibility when its HTTP responses are intentionally delayed |
| No new experiment appears | Check Product Service and Monitoring Service logs, wait for detection and database logging, then refresh |
| PowerShell command returns connection refused | Confirm the corresponding Spring Boot application is running on the expected port |

